  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Evaluate the definite Improper Integral</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Evaluate the Integral below and determine if it converges or diverges.</p>
<p>Note: \( \infty\) is entered as <b>inf</b> and \( -\infty\) is entered as <b>minf</b>.</p>
<p>\( &nbsp;\displaystyle \int_{@var_z@}^{@upper_limit@}{@func@}\,dz\)</p>
[[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]<p></p>
<p>Therefore,the integral  [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3><b>Worked solution</b></h3>
<p>Since there is a discontinuity in the integrand at \(z={@var_z@}\),we can eliminate it as follows,</p>
<p>\( \displaystyle \int_{@var_z@}^{@upper_limit@}{@func@}\,dz= \displaystyle \lim_{t \to \ {@var_z@}^{+} }\int_{t}^{@upper_limit@}{@func@}\,dz\)</p>
<p>Using substitution</p>
 <p>let  \(\quad u={@den_const+coeff_z*z@}.\) Then  \(\frac{du}{dz} ={@den_diff@}.\) So \(dz={@1/den_diff@}du\)</p>
<p>\(z \rightarrow {@upper_limit@}: \quad u \rightarrow {@den_const+coeff_z*upper_limit@}\)</p>
<p>\(z \rightarrow t: \quad u \rightarrow {@den_const+coeff_z*t@}\)</p>
<p>Hence,</p>
<p>
\(
\begin{align}
    \displaystyle \int_{t}^{{@upper_limit@}}{@func@} \,dz &amp;={@1/den_diff@}\int_{{@den_const+coeff_z*t@}}^{{@den_const+coeff_z*upper_limit@}} \frac{{@num@}}{u}du\\   
 &amp;={@num/den_diff@} \ln ({@den_const+coeff_z*upper_limit@})-{@num/den_diff@} \ln |{@den_const+coeff_z*t@}| 
    \end{align}
\)
</p>  
<p>We recall \(\displaystyle\lim_{X \to \ {0}^{+} }{\ln (X)}=- \infty \) </p>
<p>Therefore,</p>
<p>
\[
\begin{align}
\displaystyle\int_{@var_z@}^{@upper_limit@}{@func@}\,dz &amp;=\lim_{t \to \ {@var_z@}^{+} }({@ta_d@})\\
&amp;={@ta_1@}
\end{align}
\]
</p>
<p>Therefore,the integral is {@mcq_correct(ta_4)[1]@}</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
